  "body": "After reading #7896 & #7935, it looks like `blocking` attribute with value `render` is not supported by `link` elements with `preload` or `modulepreload` values. I have tested it on chrome and following code is not render blocking:\r\n```html\r\n\t<link blocking=\"render\" rel=\"preload\" as=\"font\" type=\"font/woff2\" crossorigin href=\"https://data.atonline.net/~jwt/eyJhY3QiOiJnZXQiLCJpbiI6eyJkbCI6dHJ1ZX0sInAiOiJibG9ic3JjL2Jsb2JzLWJlczdzYi1tc3ZyLWYyaGMtdnBpYS14ZjR0cHkyaSJ9/classes.woff2?v=1&u=phplatform&e=1669302816&s=7qDOLlvH1ZSbKwrT3XDpdlOkc6Cx96s2mTavfkDVBYs\">\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever [spec says the following](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#attr-link-blocking):\r\n```\r\nThe blocking attribute is a blocking attribute. It is used by link types modulepreload, preload and stylesheet, and it must only be specified on link elements that have a rel attribute containing one of those keywords.\r\n```\r\n\r\nI find it very confusing. Shouldn't it say `It is used by link type stylesheet, and it must be only...`? If so, I can file a PR if you wish.",
